course: dictionary
lesson: 9767
title: Supreme: the highest of all
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Supreme means highest in rank or power, or greatest and most important. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The Supreme Court is the highest court in the land.» The word highest in the same sentence tells you that supreme means at the very top.
explain: Supreme can also mean very great. «She made a supreme effort and won the race.» An effort is trying hard, so supreme here means very great. Check by swapping in very great: «She made a very great effort and won the race» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: In the phrase «reign supreme», supreme means the best, with no rival. A champion who reigns supreme is so good that nobody can beat them. When you see supreme, ask: is it about rank, about being greatest, or about having no rival?
fact: Supreme means highest in rank or power, or greatest and most important.
fact: «Supreme» can describe a noun, as in «supreme leader», or be part of a phrase such as «reign supreme».
fact: «Supreme Court» is the highest court in the USA, Canada, the UK, Ireland and elsewhere; Australia calls its top court the High Court.
fact: The King is the «Supreme Governor» of the Church of England, which means he is its highest leader.
fact: In 1893 the US Supreme Court still ruled the tomato a vegetable for tax, even though a botanist calls it a fruit.
exercise: «The Supreme Court is the highest court in the land.» What does supreme mean here? | Very small | Lost | *Highest in rank or power | Very slow
exercise: «She made a supreme effort and won the race.» What does supreme mean here? | Very cold | *Very great | Quiet | Last
exercise: Ella says «The lion reigns supreme over the savannah.» Which phrase means the same as reigns supreme? | Is lost in the grass | Is small and quiet | *Is the best, with no rival | Is sleeping
test: The King is the «Supreme Governor» of the Church of England. In this phrase, what does supreme mean? | Shortest | Lowest in rank | *Highest in rank or power | Very small
test: What does «supreme champion» mean? | *The greatest champion, the best of all | A champion who is tired | A champion who came last | A champion who wears a hat
exam: Mia says supreme means very small. Is she right? | Yes, it means very small | Yes, it means lost | No, it means very quiet | *No, supreme means highest or greatest
